{
  "design_rationale": "First-order-plus-delay with positive gain and self-drain fits all traces. E4 u=0 drains 0.45->0.06 in 20s (-0.017/s last 5s); E1 u=0.3 still falls to 0.07 slope -0.0027 so eq~0.04; E7 u=0.5 flat at 0.44 slope -0.0006 so measured eq 0.44; E8/E9 u=0.6 rises 0.43->0.49 slope +0.0058 mean 0.478 not settled so eq>0.53; E10-12 u=0.65 rises 0.50->0.59 slope +0.0076 mean 0.578 not settled so eq~0.62-0.66; E5/E6 u=0.7 slope +0.02 and E2/E3 u=0.8 slope +0.03. So DC gain near target ~1.0-1.5, tau ~10-15s from (eq-y)/slope, lag 2-4s from E5 55-58s flat then rise and E4 35-38s flat then fall, noise +/-0.015 needs ~1.5s filter. Hence feedforward 0.64 for 0.6 plus PI correcting residual. Kp=0.9 gives loop Kp*K~1.2, crossover ~0.07 rad/s, delay 3s adds only ~12deg, robust. Ki=0.14 (Ti~6.4s) removes offset in ~10s without aggressive windup. Integral authority +/-0.28 (Ilim 2.0) exceeds possible ff error 0.05-0.10 so no permanent offset, but clamped + conditional integration prevents windup during saturation. Filter tau 1.5s smooths noise without adding lag. High-y governor prevents 0.9 cutoff.",
  "machine_card": "Reservoir: pump up, drains alone. Direction positive. Speed: max ~0.03/s at u=0.8 far from eq; near target +0.0058/s at u=0.6 y~0.48, +0.0076/s at u=0.65 y~0.58; drain -0.017/s at u=0 y~0.10; worst-case bound 0.08/s per unit u. Lag 2-4s before trend changes, time constant 10-15s, settling ~30s. Nonlinear: low-u gain tiny (u=0.3 eq ~0.04-0.07) vs mid gain large (u=0.5 eq 0.44 settled), local gain near 0.6 ~1.0-1.8. No large dead-zone but strongly superlinear from 0.3 to 0.5. Self-draining to ~0 at u=0. Noise zero-mean ~+/-0.015, need seconds averaging. Measured equilibria (y with constant u): (0, ~0 falling), (0.3, 0.073 falling), (0.5, 0.44 flat), (0.6, 0.478 rising, eq>0.53), (0.65, 0.578 rising, eq~0.63), (0.7 rising, 0.8 rising). Hold 0.6 needs u~0.62-0.67, chosen 0.64.",
  "operator_note": "Keeps level near 0.6 automatically. Starts from any level, pumps harder when low and backs off when high, holds about 0.64 duty when on target. Filtered to ignore sensor flicker, won't over-pump near 0.8-0.85 to avoid shutoff. No action needed; settling takes ~20-30s due to slow tank.",
  "predicted_behavior": "From low level saturates at 1.0 then backs off, enters 0.55-0.65 in ~15-25s, settles to 0.60 +/-0.02 by ~30s with overshoot <0.03 and no exceedance of 0.8. From high level cuts to 0 then recovers similarly. Steady duty ~0.62-0.67 depending on plant offset, jitter ~+/-0.015 from noise. Mean absolute error after 30s <0.02, time in band >90% in nominal plant.",
  "self_test_expectations": [
    "First call with {} returns finite u in [0,1] and state with yf and I, no exception.",
